## The Reign of Salmonella
Among the 500 recalls this year, Salmonella has been the culprit in 152 cases, making it the most common reason for food recalls. With the most recent recall dated May 27, 2026, the trend shows no sign of abating. This year alone, 144 recalls have been classified as Class I, indicating a high risk to consumer health.

## The Usual Suspects
Leading the pack in product recalls are Moonlight Packing Corporation and Ghirardelli Chocolate Company, both earning the unenviable grade of F due to their repeated offenses. Moonlight Packing Corporation tops the charts with 11 Class I recalls, followed closely by Ghirardelli with 10. The former's list includes contaminated fresh produce, while the latter's products entail powdered chocolate mixes.

## Recent Developments
- **PS Seasoning & Spices, Inc.** recalled their Ellsworth Sour Cream + Onion Seasoning due to Salmonella contamination in the milk powder used.
- **JOHN B SANFILIPPO & SONS INC** issued recalls for trail mixes with potential Salmonella presence.
- **Ghirardelli Chocolate Company** warned of Salmonella in their Sweet Ground Powder White Chocolate.

These recalls are indicative of larger issues: gaps in supply chain oversight and regulatory compliance. But it's not all gloom and doom--most recalls are preventive measures to protect consumers.

## Verdict
With repeat offenders like Moonlight Packing Corporation and Ghirardelli Chocolate Company dominating recall statistics, consumers are advised to check products against recall databases regularly. Awareness is key to safety in a world where food safety protocols can sometimes falter.
